{#
/**
 * @file
 * Article card — the rows of the /articles View.
 *
 * That View uses the `entity:node` row plugin, which means there is no Views
 * row template at all: this node template is the only place the rows can be
 * shaped. Renders the shared `article-card` SDC, which owns the markup, styles
 * and props contract; this template's only job is mapping node fields onto it.
 *
 * The scalar props come from src/Hook/ArticleHooks.php rather than being read
 * out of `node.field_*` here, so the field names live in one place and this
 * template stays a mapping rather than a query.
 *
 * - The hero image goes into the `media` slot as a rendered field so its image
 *   style, alt text and cacheability are preserved; a placeholder fills the
 *   slot when field_hero is empty, which is every article today.
 * - Topic terms go into the `tags` slot as `tag-pill` atoms — components inside
 *   a slot, the thing a prop cannot express.
 *
 * @see template_preprocess_node()
 * @see \Drupal\flavourful\Hook\ArticleHooks
 */
#}
{#
  Every value here comes from ArticleHooks, never from `node.field_*` — see
  \Drupal\flavourful\NodeFieldTrait for why reading a field in Twig is not safe
  when it may be empty.

  The trailing `|filter` drops the nulls a sparse article produces (no story
  type, no summary). SDC treats an absent optional prop and one passed as null
  differently: a prop declared `type: string` rejects the null outright.
  Filtering is what lets this map stay flat instead of becoming a chain of
  `{% if %}`-guarded merges, one per field an article might not have.
#}
{% set card_props = {
  title: label,
  url: url,
  eyebrow: article_eyebrow,
  summary: article_summary,
  meta: article_meta,
  heading_level: card_heading_level|default(3),
  variant: card_variant|default('compact'),
}|filter(v => v is not null) %}

{#
  `only` keeps this template's context out of the component, so anything the
  blocks below need is passed explicitly. Without it, a node variable sharing a
  prop name (`title`, `label`, `content`) would silently override what is set
  above.

  The node's own `attributes` are passed on purpose: in this view mode the card
  is the node's entire rendered output, so node--type-article and the
  contextual-links data belong on it.
#}
{% embed 'flavourful:article-card' with card_props|merge({
  attributes: attributes,
  hero_media: content.field_hero,
  tag_items: article_tags,
}) only %}
  {% block media %}
    {% if hero_media|render|trim is not empty %}
      {{ hero_media }}
    {% else %}
      <span class="article-card__placeholder" aria-hidden="true">◍</span>
    {% endif %}
  {% endblock %}

  {#
    `tag_items`, not `tags` — the component's own slot is called `tags`, and a
    context variable of the same name would shadow it inside the component.
  #}
  {% block tags %}
    {% for tag in tag_items %}
      {{ include('flavourful:tag-pill', {
        label: tag.label,
        url: tag.url,
      }, with_context = false) }}
    {% endfor %}
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
